On Tuesday, December 1, 2015 at 1:40:47 AM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:
> This is the multivariate probit, not the multinomial.
> That means it's a latent multivariate normal.  I don't
> know how to write the density down directly, but I'm
> certainly open to suggestions.

Multivariate probit and multinomial probit have the same limitation: the lack of a good way to do general multivariate normal integrals. This is particularly a problem for Stan because the way people usually evaluate multivariate normal integrals is with a Gibbs sampler ...

