No, no, the marginal _posterior_ distributions.  This,

Omega_b[1,2]      0.268

just gives the posterior mean but gives no indication of
the posterior variance.  What, for example, are the 5% and
95% quantiles?  I would not be surprised if that range
includes the true value of 0.6.

