Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/h5Z45EYMH9o/m/Y_JKCKSxAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I have an issue with this estimation. I can't understand why Stan is not running.

This model is simple, just a bernoulli distribution of 5 coins.

Could you help me?

This is the code (in R):

# Generate data for 5 coins ( g) and the values (y : head(0) or tail(1) )
tt_dados <- data.frame(y=c(
  rbinom(300, 1, .234),
  rbinom(300, 1, .728),
  rbinom(300, 1, .534),
  rbinom(300, 1, .349),
  rbinom(300, 1, .765)),
  g=c(rep(1,300),
      rep(2,300),
      rep(3,300),
      rep(4,300),
      rep(5,300))
)

# Prepare data for Stan
t_dados <- list(
  y=tt_dados$y,
  g=tt_dados$g)

# Model
stan_st <- "
  data {
    int y[1500];
    int g[1500];
  }
  parameters {
    real x[5];
  }
  model {
    for (i in 1:1500) {
      y[i] ~ bernoulli(x[g[i]]);
    }
    for (i in 1:5) {
      x[i] ~ normal(0, 1);
    }
  }

  "
fit <- stan(model_code=stan_st, data=t_dados, iter=1500, warmup=100, thin=10, chains=2)

"

