Hi Bob, yes I've got my questions answered for the most part. It's been a useful discussion in that I've learned a lot. I think it's worth noting that ADMB coupled AD and static HMC <http://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10556788.2011.597854> (using inverse Hessian as mass matrix) probably a decade ago and there's a community of scientists that are used to its way of doing things, who likely will migrate over to Stan. I think it's worthwhile for those users (me included, obviously) to be able to notice/understand the differences and improvements to ease that transition.

I look forward to Stan 3 to see the changes. In the meantime I've got my original questions answered.

Thanks
Cole

